WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.667
We're hanging out with Florence
Pugh, ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:04.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:08.501
Now, Florence, we love getting
to know our guests

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.000
here at "The Tonight Show"
and I thought it would be fun

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.300
to do it while playing a game.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.000
It's time to play "Guest Test."

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.167
Here we go.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.567
-♪ Tonight Show guest test,
yeah ♪

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:19.767
-Here's how it works.
Before the show, you answered

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.234
a series of questions about
things that you like.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.767
-Yep.
-And now the audience is

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.334
going to try
to guess your answers.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.300
Everyone has clickers
at their seats.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.734
So, you can vote answers A or B.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.567
Okay, we're going to do
five questions.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.734
And here's the deal.
If our audience gets at least

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:37.133
three questions right,
everyone gets a free pint of

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.534
Tonight Dough Ben and Jerry's
ice cream.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:44.567
So, yeah, you guys --
-I'm sorry if it doesn't

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:47.534
work out your way, guys, because
that's a good prize.

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.367
-Yeah, people are going to be
really disappointed, yeah.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.467
Because it was going so well.
-I know.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.801
-The interview was great.
We loved you.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:53.901
We gave you a standing ovation.

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.200
Now, who knows
what's going to happen.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.400
-They're going to throw
ice cream at me.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.801
-"We want ice cream."

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.534
Alright, here we go.
This first question --

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.133
I don't know the answers either,
so I'm not --

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.367
these aren't rigged.
What is your favorite '90s song?

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:09.501
Is it, A, "Blue (Da Ba Dee),"
Eiffel 65.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.834
♪ I'm blue, da ba dee
da bu die ♪

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.968
Okay.
Or is it "Barbie Girl" by Aqua?

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.601
♪ I'm a Barbie girl ♪

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:21.701
[ Humming ]

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.434
Hmm. I'm going to vote too.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.000
Quest, you're voting too?
Tariq, you're voting?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.334
What do you think it is?

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.167
I think I'm going to say it's
"Blue (Da Ba Dee)."

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:32.467
-Are we talking about my fave?
-No, we're picking Florence's.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.367
-Yeah, sure, your favorite.
-Florence's favorite.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:37.067
-Ah. I got to go with my own.
I'm "Barbie Girl" all day.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:39.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.667
-Alright.
Let's see the audience results.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.467
The audience chose...

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.601
"Barbie Girl."

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.100
Uh-oh. Florence, tell us

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.434
what is your favorite song
from the '90s.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.067
-It's "Blue."

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:54.901
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.000
Hang on, there's a reason.
-Why?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.167
-I'm 10 years younger than my
older sister, and when that was

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.267
happening, my older sister
was playing it all the time.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.801
And I thought this was,
like, the disco tune.

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:06.667
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.200
-And so I'd walk past her room

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.868
and I'm like...
[ Humming ]

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:14.300
And so, that's just been
in my head.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.767
-Alright, alright.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.834
We're 0 for 1 for audience, but
we are getting to know you.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.200
-Yes.
-Yeah, which I love.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.033
-Most important thing.
-That's the important, yeah.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.334
Just to know each other.
That's all we really want.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.434
More than ice cream.
It's friendship.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:31.601
What is your favorite
Florence Pugh movie?

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:32.901
This is a tricky question
to ask you.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:34.734
-Yeah, this was a weird one
because I don't watch

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.467
my own movies,
like, on the regular.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:39.234
I'm not like,
"Ooh, it's Friday night.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.167
I'll watch my own movie."

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:44.834
-Is it "Midsommar"
or is it "Lady Macbeth"?

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.667
-It's a hard one. This is
a weird question as well.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.901
-Yeah, this is a tricky one
for me.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:55.334
I mean --
-Stumped?

00:02:55.334 --> 00:03:00.133
-Yeah, I'm going to say
"Midsommar."

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.601
I'm going to say,
A, "Midsommar."

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.167
Tariq, what are you thinking
on this?

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.567
-I'm going to go, you know, just
because you said, "Midsommar,"

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.734
I'm going to go "Lady Macbeth."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.167
-You going to go the opposite?
-Yeah, man.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.767
-Crowd, are you leaning one way
or the other?

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:14.501
[ Audience says "Midsommar" ]
-"Midsommar."

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.033
The audience is saying
"Midsommar."

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.734
What are we saying right here?
Audience, what do you think?

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:21.234
[ Audience shouting ]
Let's see the results.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:24.701
-Oh!

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:25.868
-It's very, very close.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:27.467
-You were so close!

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.234
It's "Lady Macbeth"!
[ Audience ohs ]

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.834
[ Sad tuba ]

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:34.334
-Are you doing it on purpose?
Are you doing it on purpose?

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.133
-Hang on, hang on, hang on.
Okay.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.033
The question was, which one --
I didn't understand what it was.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.634
Like, do I want to watch them
or did I enjoy being in them?

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:45.300
And because it was such a weird,
small-budget movie

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.834
and I appreciated what it did
for me and my career,

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:50.100
I chose "Lady Macbeth,"
but now I'm sorry.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:54.033
-Alright, here's the thing.
So, we have two -- alright,

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.100
we need to get these next
three completely right.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.567
-Yeah, guys.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.300
-If the audience is going to go
home with ice cream tonight.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.901
We've got to really focus up,
guys!

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:04.501
[ Cheers ]

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:06.801
Think. We are Florence Pugh.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:09.534
We are in Florence's brain.
Ready?

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:12.200
What is your favorite color?

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:17.434
Is it, A, rusty orange?

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:20.868
Or is it, B, sky blue?

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:23.968
I think -- I'm going to say
rusty orange.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:28.367
I'm feeling -- Florence, I think
sky blue is too common for you.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.000
-Yeah, it's a bit --
it's -- I don't know.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.601
I'm not saying anything.
-Yeah, okay.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.400
But you almost said something.
-I did, and I'm so sorry.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.000
-Guys, did you --
alright, did you hear that?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.834
Are you paying attention?
-I said nothing.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.701
-Alright, I'm going to say
rusty orange.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.067
Let's see the results.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.234
Audience, what is Florence's
favorite color?

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.067
Rusty orange?
-No!

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.133
-Is the answer?
-Yes!

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:48.334
-Yes!
[ Ding ]

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.133
-We want to get ice cream.
Alright.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.467
-We got one.
-I do love rusty orange.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.400
-Me too, especially when it's
actual rust.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.601
-Ooh, yeah.
-Yeah, and you shouldn't touch

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.234
it because you might get
ill and die.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.767
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.801
The dangerous color.
Yeah, exactly.

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.868
I want my colors
to be dangerous.

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.200
Alright. Here we go.
-Fiery red.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.868
-Yes, ooh!

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.400
What is your favorite way
to relax?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.133
Is it, A, a massage
and then audio book?

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:22.701
Or is it, B, a bath
and "Real Housewives"?

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.000
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:30.667
-I mean, you -- it says bath
and "Real Housewives."

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:33.601
I think massage and audio book
is not --

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:35.601
Your favorite way to relax?

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.534
A bath and "Real Housewives" is
unbelievable.

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:41.267
If you really watch "Real
Housewives," it is relaxing.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:42.934
I'm going to say it's --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:44.801
I do. I love it.
Because you know what?

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.701
I go, "It's not my problem."
-Yeah.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:47.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.167
I don't have to deal with that.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.000
-I don't have to deal with that.
That's none of my business.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.501
And that's why I love it, so I'm
going to go B on this one.

00:05:53.501 --> 00:05:55.000
Tariq, what do you think?

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.634
-Dude, definitely
massage and audio book.

00:05:57.634 --> 00:05:59.300
-Massage and audio book?

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.167
It sounds like you're doing
too many things at once.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:05.067
Pressing play and pause.
Loud, up, harder, softer.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:06.701
Too much involved.

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:08.033
Bath and "Real Housewives,"
what do you guys think?

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.167
Audience, let's see the results.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:10.367
[ Audience shouts B ]

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:13.667
Bath and "Real Housewives"?

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:14.801
-Yes!
[ Ding! ]

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:16.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:20.767
-One more to go! One more to go!

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:26.300
-You're so right though.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.968
It really is so relaxing knowing

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:32.267
that you don't have to
deal with that or this.

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:34.667
-No. It's none of my business.
-None of my business.

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:37.968
But I can sit in the bath
and drink my wine

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:40.400
and go mwah!
-I love that.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.901
Alright. This is the last one.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.000
This is for Ben and Jerry's
ice cream

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.667
for everyone in the audience.
[ Cheers ]

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.000
Ooh!

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.133
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:52.367
You're kneeling on your chair.
-I'm excited.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:54.868
I'm freaking out.
This is, like, a big deal.

00:06:54.868 --> 00:06:56.334
Do you know how many people
would be happy

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:57.434
if they get this right?
[ Cheers ]

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:59.934
-Yeah, and you'll now
really know me.

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:02.834
-And I feel like --
Already I feel like I know you.

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:05.501
But here we go. What is
your favorite pizza topping?

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:06.667
-Oh.
[ Audience ohs ]

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:08.467
Oh, no.
-But this is tricky because

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:11.133
you're from England.
-Yeah.

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:12.834
Well, what?
That doesn't mean anything.

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:15.067
[ Laughter ]
I still have taste.

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:17.400
-I know, but there's
different rules there.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:19.934
-Oh, I see.

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.834
-Is it, A -- it can't be this.

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:24.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.968 --> 00:07:27.367
A, ham and pineapple.

00:07:27.367 --> 00:07:30.834
Or, B, sausage and mushrooms.

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:34.267
Ooh, silence.

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:36.234
'Cause I've been to England
a bunch of times.

00:07:36.234 --> 00:07:38.801
And I feel like
ham and pineapple

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:40.734
are, like, Americanized.

00:07:40.734 --> 00:07:42.767
They brought that over there
and people got used to it.

00:07:42.767 --> 00:07:44.267
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:45.701
Let's think sausage.

00:07:45.701 --> 00:07:47.634
[ English accent ] 'Ello.
Say it. Sausage.

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:49.267
Sausage. That's how they say it.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:51.167
Sausage.

00:07:51.167 --> 00:07:53.701
You don't say ham and pineapple.

00:07:53.701 --> 00:07:56.434
You go sausage.
'Ey! Oi!

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:58.701
-Oi!
-Oi, sausage.

00:07:58.701 --> 00:08:00.167
[ Normal voice ]
You yell at people.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.801
You get it. [English accent]
'Ey, sausage and mushroom!

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:04.834
Yell it!
[Normal voice] I think it is --

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:06.467
-Are you using your tongue
when you speak or not?

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:07.667
-No. Not at all.

00:08:07.667 --> 00:08:09.634
[ English accent ]
It's sausage and mushroom!

00:08:09.634 --> 00:08:11.100
[ Normal voice ]
And you yell it at people.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.567
Guys, I think --
What are we thinking here?

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:15.534
[ Audience shouts B ]

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:17.601
We got to vote. Come on.

00:08:17.601 --> 00:08:18.901
I want ice cream so bad.

00:08:18.901 --> 00:08:21.234
Let's see the results.

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:22.801
Sausage and mushroom.
-Yes!

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:24.367
-Is that correct?
[ Dinging ]

00:08:24.367 --> 00:08:27.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes! Ice cream!

00:08:27.133 --> 00:08:28.400
Come on!

00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:34.300
Sausage and mushroom!

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:35.968
Ice cream for everybody!

00:08:35.968 --> 00:08:38.100
Tonight Dough and Florence Pugh!

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.434
"A Good Person" hits theaters
this Friday!

00:08:40.434 --> 00:08:42.133
We'll be right back
with Gaten Matarazzo.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:43.467
Stick around, everybody.

